    "answer": {
      "short": "$0$ intersections.\n\nThe distance between centres is $2\\sqrt{10}>4+2$, so the circles are separate.",
      "worked": "The centres are $(-2,1)$ and $(4,-1)$, with radii $r_1=4$ and $r_2=2$ respectively.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}d&=\\sqrt{(4-(-2))^2+(-1-1)^2}\\\\d&=2\\sqrt{10}\\\\r_1+r_2&=6\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $d^2=40>36=(r_1+r_2)^2$, the distance between centres exceeds the sum of the radii. The circles are separate, so there are $0$ intersections.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
